WEBVTT

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:08.330
You were so angry yesterday,
so why didn't you even do it today?

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:12.000
Because... the ribbon is cute and I don't like that.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:13.830
You don't like cute stuff?

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.540
It's kind of uncharacteristic of me...

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:18.500
But you like things like stuffed dolls, right?

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.000
Like that phone strap!

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.950
This is fine! It's not all that cute.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.660
It's not cute, huh?

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:27.370
Well?

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.620
Still no change from earlier.

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:31.870
She sure is miserable.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:35.370
I am miserable.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:38.830
What exactly does a campaign manager have to do?

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:45.040
Uh, well, senpai and I will hand out fliers,
and posters and stuff together...

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:50.000
It sounds annoying, but if you're doing that much,
what if you think of it as continuing to help?

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.620
Hm, that makes sense, but...

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:57.450
There's also a campaign speech at an assembly
in front of the entire student body...

00:00:57.750 --> 00:01:00.580
Whoa! That sounds demanding!

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.040
Yuu, don't you hate standing in front of a crowd?

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.120
You should turn her down.

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:07.910
I do!

00:01:07.910 --> 00:01:10.750
I say that I don't want to be responsible for
something so important.

00:01:11.290 --> 00:01:14.450
But Nanami-senpai just won't give up.

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:17.160
She really likes you, huh?

00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:18.830
But why, though?

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:19.950
Who knows.

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.700
Isn't Saeki-senpai almost always with Nanami-senpai?

00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:37.450
First Semester Exams
Year 2 Top-Ranked

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:37.450
Student Results
Class 3   Class 1   Class 1
Class 7   Class 2
Sayaka    Touko
Saeki    Nanami
Ai     Minoru   Nobuyuki
Itoh  Mitarashi  Yamanaka

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:37.500
They say that ever since they entered
this school they've kept this ranking.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:46.200
They draw attention just walking side by side,
and if she wants to win an election,

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:49.120
there's a much better choice than me...

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:53.910
Because I think I'm falling in love with you...

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.540
No, no, no...

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:37.540
Ready!

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:38.750
Here it comes!

00:03:38.750 --> 00:03:40.080
You can do it!

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.200
Over here!

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:52.330
Nice serve!

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:53.790
Alright, Touko!

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.080
You're amazing!

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.250
Thanks!

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:03.870
Sorry, can I take a breather?

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:08.750
Sayaka?

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:11.370
Looks like you're in quite a good mood.

00:04:11.950 --> 00:04:13.370
I said I was sorry!

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:15.000
Cheer up.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:21.830
Whatever... Of course I'm in a bad mood, it's just
that I assumed that I'd be serving as your manager.

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:25.750
I apologize for not talking to you about it first!

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.200
Just like this!

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:29.450
But...

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:31.040
But?

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.830
I really do want to ask Koito to do it.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:37.330
Why?

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:39.450
What do you mean, "Why?"

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:46.200
I'm sure she's fairly capable of the job
and she'd be a good fit for the position,

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:50.000
but I honestly don't understand.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:54.750
Are you thinking seriously about the election?

00:04:54.750 --> 00:04:58.290
Aren't you being a bit careless in saying
that you'll definitely win the election like this?

00:04:58.290 --> 00:04:59.830
I'm not though!

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:06.910
Ah! Touko! Can you get that?

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:11.330
I think that there's meaning
in being recommended by a first year.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:15.370
Don't you think May is too early to have an election?

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:19.790
The first years know basically nothing about
the second year candidates, right?

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:22.080
That's true...

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:27.500
If there are first years participating in the election
that think they can't relate to anything,

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:29.370
I think we can catch their attention.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:34.040
Besides, I want the contents of the speech
to not to just praise me,

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.580
I want to have an honest, straightforward opinion.

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:42.200
If we do that, it will have a profound appeal
on whoever listens to her, right?

00:05:42.580 --> 00:05:44.580
I think it's not too bad of a plan.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:52.250
What will you do if you're elected?

00:05:52.830 --> 00:05:57.200
Not that it's decided, but I plan
to ask her to become an officer.

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:00.620
That's why I want to start building
a trusting relationship now.

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:03.040
I see.

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:09.540
In other words, you want to have deeper
trust in that girl than you do in me, huh?

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:10.450
Huh?

00:06:19.790 --> 00:06:20.500
Sayaka!

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:22.200
Touko!

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.700
Alright!

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:33.410
Both you and Touko are awesome! You're so in sync!

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:39.160
Don't you think our trust in each other
is deep enough already?

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.580
Jeez. Since you're so unfair...

00:06:44.410 --> 00:06:47.500
I guess I have to. I'll give in to you.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:49.250
Thanks!

00:06:50.160 --> 00:06:53.250
But if you lose now, I'm gonna be angry.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.950
I've got this. I'll absolutely show you
that I'll become president.

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:58.200
So...

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:01.040
I look forward to working with you, Vice President.

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:08.950
We're changing classrooms next, right?

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:10.080
Yeah.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:12.660
Yuu?

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:14.040
Yuu?

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:14.870
Huh?

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.540
Senpai?

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:22.580
Here.

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:24.620
What's this?

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:26.830
It's a draft for the campaign speech.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:31.370
I wrote it as a rough copy for me to read,
so you probably can't use it as is...

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:35.700
But you can quote parts of it or
it can be a reference, so use it as you'd like.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:39.120
But I don't know if I'll be able to do a good job!

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:41.910
I'm sure you'd do much better...

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:44.370
That's most likely true.

00:07:44.790 --> 00:07:48.000
However, since it's you there
are certain things that can be done.

00:07:48.370 --> 00:07:51.330
At the very least, it looks like Touko thinks that way.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:54.870
But...

00:07:55.370 --> 00:07:57.410
Please take care of her, okay?

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:10.000
If even Saeki-senpai says that...

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:14.700
I understand. I'll do what I can.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:23.700
Candidate
Year 2 Class 1   Touko Nanami
Head Teacher   Atsuko Tsuji
Homeroom Teacher   Masahiro Kobori

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:23.700
Campaign Manager
Year 1 Class 1   Yuu Koito 
Head Teacher   Kiyoshi Aoyama

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:23.660
With this, we'll become partners that
fight together in the election, right?

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.120
I suppose so.

00:08:27.540 --> 00:08:29.080
I'm looking forward to working with you, Koito!

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:34.750
I'll do everything I can,
but please give me support, okay?

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:36.450
It's fine, it's fine!

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:41.370
Nanami-senpai, I didn't know
you could be such a pushy person.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:45.120
That's because I absolutely wanted you to do this.

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:48.620
Why would you go that far for...

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:50.160
Huh?

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:52.120
Nothing.

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:53.370
What is it?

00:08:57.080 --> 00:08:58.040
Well...

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.500
What was that thing the other day?

00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:04.700
The other day?

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:08.830
"I think I'm falling in love with you..."

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:11.910
That was...

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:18.080
Uh, sorry about that. I made you worry, huh?

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:20.500
I wouldn't say "worry..."

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:26.620
I don't even know myself. I guess I just blurted
something out, and I spoke before thinking...

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:30.450
Ah, I know you didn't mean it in a weird way, though.

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:35.000
We're both girls anyway, so...

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:42.750
Well, even if we weren't both girls,
I'm not the type who falls in love anyway...

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:46.080
Senpai?

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:48.950
Please don't make sudden stops like that.

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:57.080
Sen...

00:09:58.580 --> 00:09:59.540
pai?

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:31.540
My "love" is...

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:34.080
a love where I want to do something like this.

00:10:37.620 --> 00:10:40.660
My heart races when I'm with you.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:48.790
I've never had this feeling with anyone before.

00:11:13.370 --> 00:11:14.910
What do I do?

00:11:16.750 --> 00:11:17.950
That's...

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:21.040
what I want to ask.

00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:26.870
Heating Up

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:31.950
Application for First Love

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:43.540
It's perfect.

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:47.040
It's definitely a lie that this was a first draft.

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:51.950
I didn't know there were this many people
helping with the election.

00:11:51.950 --> 00:11:54.620
Maki-kun, you came!

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:58.250
I was hoping I could help lighten
the burden on the manager at least a little.

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:00.700
Thank you!

00:12:01.580 --> 00:12:02.750
Touko, you're late.

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:04.540
Sorry I kept you waiting!

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:07.500
How could the lead role be late for their entrance?

00:12:07.500 --> 00:12:09.040
I said I was sorry!

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:15.870
Thank you all for gathering here today.

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:18.200
Starting tomorrow we'll be working on campaigning,

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:21.830
so today, I'd like to hold a simple introduction meeting.

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:30.830
Are there any other questions?

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:32.120
47th Student Council
Presidential Election Schedule

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:32.160
No questions!

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:35.200
Okay then, that will be it for today.

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:39.410
We're all going to be busy doing various things,
but I look forward to working with everyone.

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:44.660
Great work today!

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:46.830
Uh, yeah, thank you.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:51.290
Koito.

00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:56.290
Do you have a minute?

00:13:06.830 --> 00:13:08.200
Sorry about before.

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:11.750
It's alright, I wasn't bothered by it.

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:13.790
Well, but, that was...

00:13:25.580 --> 00:13:27.200
Really, I'm sorry.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:32.910
But that's not the reason I asked you to be my manager.

00:13:40.080 --> 00:13:42.660
It really isn't the reason, right?

00:13:43.500 --> 00:13:45.660
Yeah. And so,

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:50.660
can I ask you to do it once again,
as a friend who's campaigning with me?

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:55.160
Alright.

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:57.080
Really?

00:13:57.830 --> 00:14:02.410
I did say I would do it once,
and since Saeki-senpai is also depending on me...

00:14:06.660 --> 00:14:07.870
I'll do it.

00:14:08.790 --> 00:14:09.950
Thanks!

00:14:13.120 --> 00:14:15.790
It honestly didn't bother me.

00:14:17.950 --> 00:14:21.500
To have it suddenly stolen by a girl like that...

00:14:22.790 --> 00:14:25.080
it's something I should hate, right?

00:14:27.290 --> 00:14:29.870
But if I don't hate it, then...

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:36.500
can't I feel more excited about it?

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:39.620
My first kiss.

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:44.830
I didn't... feel a thing.

00:14:52.830 --> 00:14:56.870
Since then, it hasn't happened even once...

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:07.450
Touko
Nanami

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:05.330
I'm Touko Nanami, candidate for student council
president. Thank you for your support!

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:07.370
Thanks for your support!

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:09.620
Good luck, Nanami!

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:10.790
Thank you!

00:15:11.750 --> 00:15:16.950
Student Council
Presidential Candidate
Touko
Nanami

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:13.750
Well, how'd this one turn out?

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:16.790
It's a little embarrassing...

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:19.870
There. This should do it.

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:22.620
Oh! Such beautiful writing!

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:26.200
Touko! This poster doesn't have a stamp on it!

00:15:26.200 --> 00:15:28.500
What? Did they forgot to stamp that one?

00:15:28.500 --> 00:15:33.040
Oh, then I'll go to the election management
committee teacher and be right back!

00:15:33.410 --> 00:15:34.910
Thanks, Koito!

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:39.200
Right.

00:15:39.870 --> 00:15:42.290
We're an ordinary candidate and manager.

00:15:42.910 --> 00:15:46.660
Staff Room

00:15:44.370 --> 00:15:46.700
Can I have a stamp for permission
to post this on the wall, please?

00:15:47.160 --> 00:15:49.290
Permission to Post
Election Management
Committee

00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:49.330
Okay, thanks for waiting.

00:15:49.660 --> 00:15:51.200
Thank you!

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:54.330
Thanks for your hard work. Good luck!

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:59.290
So Nanami is a candidate for the student council, huh?

00:15:59.290 --> 00:16:02.450
Yeah. Time sure does fly...

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:06.080
She must be happy about that, too.

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:12.040
Newspaper Club

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:14.700
Koito, you're the only first year student who's
also a campaign manager this time around...

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:19.910
Y-yes! I was hoping I could get all
the first years to get interested in the election

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:24.160
by telling them how Nanami-senpai is through my eyes.

00:16:24.700 --> 00:16:28.410
I see. Thank you very much. That will be all.

00:16:30.790 --> 00:16:34.000
Great work. Doing interviews is nerve racking, huh?

00:16:34.000 --> 00:16:37.120
It doesn't seem like it's like that for you, though.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:39.370
That isn't true at all.

00:16:40.200 --> 00:16:43.250
They're really serious about this election, aren't they?

00:16:40.450 --> 00:16:43.250
Now, could you say a few words in closing, please?

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:46.040
Our school goes all out for our events.

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:44.660
Okay, sure.

00:16:46.040 --> 00:16:48.790
The other candidates are really giving it their all, too.

00:16:49.200 --> 00:16:52.080
Even so, you're confident about all of this, right?

00:16:53.250 --> 00:16:54.370
I wonder...

00:16:55.870 --> 00:17:00.450
That face was so calm,
the same as the day I first met her.

00:17:02.160 --> 00:17:03.250
I knew it.

00:17:04.660 --> 00:17:10.500
That was the mistake that made me
think Nanami-senpai and I were the same,

00:17:10.950 --> 00:17:15.500
and that the special feelings
and the excitement, for sure...

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:19.700
All candidates and campaign managers,
please gather over here.

00:17:19.870 --> 00:17:20.830
Okay!

00:17:22.870 --> 00:17:23.870
Let's go!

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:29.200
Sorry, but please squeeze together a bit more.

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:31.080
And keep moving closer together, one step at a time.

00:17:32.750 --> 00:17:33.620
Sorry.

00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:35.790
Uh, yeah...

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:39.200
Okay, stop.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:43.080
I'm going to take the picture now, so everyone relax!

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:44.080
Koito?

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:47.160
What are you...

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:03.870
Up until now, when someone's said they like me,

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:06.700
it's never made my heart flutter.

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:14.660
That special feeling... I don't understand it.

00:18:21.870 --> 00:18:23.700
Okay, great job, everyone!

00:18:24.290 --> 00:18:25.620
Nice work!

00:18:32.750 --> 00:18:33.750
It's not fair.

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:41.580
I thought that Nanami-senpai was the same as I am...

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:45.830
but she made that face,
even though I just grabbed her hand.

00:18:48.200 --> 00:18:51.870
Senpai already knows that specialness.

00:18:54.500 --> 00:19:00.120
But even though... I want to get there, too...

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:19.950
Read
Thank you. Thanks for

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:19.950
your hard work too, Senpai. 
Today
I want to take some time to think about
the draft for the speech, so is tomorrow
on the way home from school okay?

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:24.500
Okay, got it... and send.

00:19:27.160 --> 00:19:28.500
I get it.

00:19:29.370 --> 00:19:33.750
I had selfish expectations,
and I'm just selfishly disappointed.

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:38.500
Senpai and I are different.

00:19:41.250 --> 00:19:43.500
That specialness won't come to me.

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.620
I'll just say it straight.

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:56.910
I'll tell Senpai that I can't fall in love with her.

00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:01.540
Please take a look.

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:03.160
This is it, huh?

00:20:03.160 --> 00:20:07.500
Yes. I tried to write notes for it in my own way for now.

00:20:10.790 --> 00:20:11.750
Um...

00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:15.370
Before all this, there's something I wa-

00:20:15.370 --> 00:20:16.580
Sorry for the wait!

00:20:17.370 --> 00:20:19.120
Which one of you ordered the café au lait?

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:20.910
Oh, me.

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:23.080
Please, take your time.

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:27.250
Koito.

00:20:27.540 --> 00:20:29.750
Oh? Uh, yes?

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:31.950
I won't ask you to go out with me...

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:33.000
Huh?

00:20:34.370 --> 00:20:37.540
I know you can't think of someone as special.

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:40.370
You also won't fall in love with me.

00:20:40.910 --> 00:20:42.000
That's okay.

00:20:50.870 --> 00:20:51.790
So...

00:20:52.450 --> 00:20:53.910
Let me love you.

00:20:57.580 --> 00:20:59.250
That's weird, though!

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:03.200
To think that even though you love someone,
you don't want them to love you back...

00:21:04.540 --> 00:21:05.700
You're right.

00:21:06.290 --> 00:21:10.830
But, maybe it's because I didn't think I could
do something like fall in love with someone.

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:15.200
Right now, I feel very fulfilled.

00:21:16.700 --> 00:21:18.950
I don't want to give up this feeling.

00:21:20.870 --> 00:21:21.950
Should I stop?

00:21:22.750 --> 00:21:24.500
I-I...

00:21:27.000 --> 00:21:28.200
I...

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:34.120
If you're okay with that...

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:38.370
then I don't mind.

00:21:42.540 --> 00:21:43.950
Thank you!

00:21:57.580 --> 00:22:01.620
I wonder... why I told her that I don't mind.

00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:05.830
This girl...

00:22:07.370 --> 00:22:09.910
really is unfair.
